        "original_id": "cf872afa-926c-5c03-812e-05174eddb6d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mariya Matveyevna Stepanova, Mikhail Glinka, Alexander Pushkin\n- Products: A Life for the Tsar, Ruslan and Lyudmila, Dmitry Donskoy\n- Concepts: opera, poem\n\nFacts:\n- Alexander Pushkin wrote the 1820 poem Ruslan and Lyudmila.\n- Mikhail Glinka composed the opera Ruslan and Lyudmila between 1837 and 1842.\n- The opera Ruslan and Lyudmila is in five acts and eight tableaux.\n- The opera Ruslan and Lyudmila is based on Alexander Pushkin's 1820 poem of the same name.\n- Mariya Matveyevna Stepanova, who lived from 1811 or 1816 to 1903, was a Russian opera singer.\n- Mariya Matveyevna Stepanova created the leading soprano roles in A Life for the Tsar, Ruslan and Lyudmila, and Dmitry Donskoy.",
